        "expression_printed_normalized": "sqrt36.48 = 6.040",
        "route_printed": "6.033 plus correction on 8 equal to 7; OR 6.042 minus correction on 2 equal to 2"
      },
      {
        "expression_printed_normalized": "sqrt886.3 = sqrt(886.3*10^2) = sqrt8.863*10 = 2.978*10 = 29.78 [first equality is printed incorrectly]",
        "route_printed": "Frozen independent pixels confirm the first right radical repeats886.3 before*10^2, while the following line uses8.863. Faithful expression retains this printing error; mathematically valid normalization requires8.863 in the first right radical. No affected answer adopts the invalid equality."
      },
